---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import { TOOLS } from '../lib/site';
import { breadcrumb, faqPage, softwareApplication, webPage } from '../lib/schema';
import { ITEM_UNITS, STATES } from '../lib/india';

const tool = TOOLS[1];
const title = 'Bill of Supply Generator — Free GST-Compliant PDF';
const description =
	'Create a GST-compliant Bill of Supply in your browser and download it as a PDF. For unregistered vendors, freelancers and composition dealers — Rule 49 fields, amount in words, no sign-up.';

const faqs = [
	{
		question: 'What is the difference between a Bill of Supply and a Tax Invoice?',
		answer:
			'A <strong>Tax Invoice</strong> is issued by a registered person for taxable supplies and shows the GST charged (CGST/SGST or IGST), which the buyer can claim as input tax credit. A <strong>Bill of Supply</strong> is issued where no tax may be charged — by composition dealers, for exempt or nil-rated supplies, and in practice by unregistered vendors — so it carries no tax column and gives the buyer no credit.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Can an unregistered vendor issue a Bill of Supply?',
		answer:
			'Strictly, the CGST Rules define the “bill of supply” for registered persons. An unregistered vendor (turnover below the ₹40 lakh goods / ₹20 lakh services threshold, lower in special-category states) cannot charge GST at all and issues a plain bill without tax. This generator produces exactly that format: no GSTIN, no tax column and a clear statement that the supplier is not registered under GST.',
	},
	{
		question: 'What must a composition dealer write on a Bill of Supply?',
		answer:
			'The words <strong>“Composition taxable person, not eligible to collect tax on supplies”</strong> must appear at the top of every bill of supply, and the dealer’s GSTIN must be shown. The generator adds both automatically when you select “Composition dealer”.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Is a Bill of Supply required for small amounts?',
		answer:
			'Under Rule 49 read with Rule 46, a registered person need not issue a bill of supply where the value is less than ₹200 and the recipient is unregistered and does not ask for one — provided a consolidated bill of supply is prepared at the end of each day for all such supplies.',
	},
];

const schema = [
	webPage({ name: title, path: tool.href, description }),
	softwareApplication({
		name: tool.name,
		path: tool.href,
		description,
		category: 'BusinessApplication',
		features: [
			'Unregistered vendor and composition dealer modes',
			'Mandatory composition declaration and GSTIN',
			'Multiple line items with HSN/SAC, quantity, unit and rate',
			'Discount and round-off',
			'Amount in words in the Indian numbering system',
			'Inter-state supply warnings',
			'A4 PDF download generated in the browser',
			'Drafts stored only on your device',
		],
		keywords: tool.keywords,
	}),
	faqPage(faqs, tool.href),
	breadcrumb([
		{ name: 'Home', path: '/' },
		{ name: tool.name, path: tool.href },
	]),
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
	<section class="border-b border-hairline bg-canvas">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-5 pt-8 pb-10 sm:px-8 sm:pt-12 sm:pb-14">
			<Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Tools', href: '/#tools' }, { name: tool.shortName }]} />
			<div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl">
				<p class="eyebrow">GST compliance · Free · No sign-up</p>
				<h1 class="mt-3 text-display text-ink">Bill of Supply Generator</h1>
				<p class="mt-4 text-lead text-ink-2">
					For unregistered vendors, freelancers and composition dealers who cannot charge GST. Fill in the details, watch the
					A4 document build itself, and download a PDF — nothing is uploaded, ever.
				</p>
			</div>
			<ul class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2" aria-label="Highlights">
				<li class="chip">Rule 49 fields</li>
				<li class="chip">Composition declaration</li>
				<li class="chip">Amount in words</li>
				<li class="chip">A4 PDF</li>
				<li class="chip">Drafts stay on your device</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="tool" class="bg-parchment pb-24 lg:pb-0" aria-labelledby="tool-heading">
		<h2 id="tool-heading" class="sr-only">Bill of Supply form and preview</h2>
		<div class="mx-auto grid max-w-page gap-6 px-5 py-8 sm:px-8 sm:py-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,30rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:items-start" data-bos-tool>
			<!-- Form -->
			<form class="card grid gap-8 p-5 sm:p-6" data-bos-form novalidate autocomplete="on">
				<!-- Supplier -->
				<fieldset class="grid gap-4">
					<legend class="text-[1.0625rem] font-semibold text-ink">1. Your business (supplier)</legend>
					<div>
						<p class="field-label">Registration status</p>
						<div class="grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
							<button type="button" data-supplier-type="unregistered" class="option-card" aria-pressed="true">
								<span class="text-caption font-semibold text-ink">Not registered under GST</span>
								<span class="text-fine text-ink-2">Below the threshold. No GSTIN, no tax charged.</span>
							</button>
							<button type="button" data-supplier-type="composition" class="option-card" aria-pressed="false">
								<span class="text-caption font-semibold text-ink">Composition dealer</span>
								<span class="text-fine text-ink-2">Registered under Section 10. GSTIN required.</span>
							</button>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div>
						<label for="supplier-name" class="field-label">Business / trade name</label>
						<input id="supplier-name" name="supplier.name" type="text" class="field" placeholder="e.g. Meera Design Studio" autocomplete="organization" />
					</div>
					<div>
						<label for="supplier-address" class="field-label">Address</label>
						<textarea id="supplier-address" name="supplier.address" rows="2" class="field" placeholder="Street, city, PIN" autocomplete="street-address"></textarea>
					</div>
					<div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
						<div>
							<label for="supplier-state" class="field-label">State</label>
							<select id="supplier-state" name="supplier.stateCode" class="field">
								{STATES.map((s) => <option value={s.code}>{s.name} ({s.code})</option>)}
							</select>
						</div>
						<div data-gstin-field hidden>
							<label for="supplier-gstin" class="field-label">GSTIN</label>
							<input id="supplier-gstin" name="supplier.gstin" type="text" class="field font-mono uppercase" maxlength="15" placeholder="27ABCDE1234F1Z5" spellcheck="false" />
						</div>
						<div>
							<label for="supplier-pan" class="field-label">PAN <span class="font-normal text-ink-3">(optional)</span></label>
							<input id="supplier-pan" name="supplier.pan" type="text" class="field font-mono uppercase" maxlength="10" placeholder="ABCDE1234F" spellcheck="false" />
						</div>
						<div>
							<label for="supplier-phone" class="field-label">Phone <span class="font-normal text-ink-3">(optional)</span></label>
							<input id="supplier-phone" name="supplier.phone" type="tel" class="field" placeholder="+91 98765 43210" autocomplete="tel" />
						</div>
						<div class="sm:col-span-2">
							<label for="supplier-email" class="field-label">Email <span class="font-normal text-ink-3">(optional)</span></label>
							<input id="supplier-email" name="supplier.email" type="email" class="field" placeholder="you@example.com" autocomplete="email" />
						</div>
					</div>
				</fieldset>

				<!-- Bill details -->
				<fieldset class="grid gap-4 border-t border-hairline pt-6">
					<legend class="float-left text-[1.0625rem] font-semibold text-ink">2. Bill details</legend>
					<div class="clear-both grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
						<div>
							<label for="bill-number" class="field-label">Bill number</label>
							<input id="bill-number" name="bill.number" type="text" class="field tnum" placeholder="BOS/2026-27/001" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" />
						</div>
						<div>
							<label for="bill-date" class="field-label">Date</label>
							<input id="bill-date" name="bill.date" type="date" class="field tnum" />
						</div>
						<div>
							<label for="bill-pos" class="field-label">Place of supply</label>
							<select id="bill-pos" name="bill.placeOfSupply" class="field">
								{STATES.map((s) => <option value={s.code}>{s.name} ({s.code})</option>)}
							</select>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p class="field-hint">Serial numbers must be unique within a financial year and no longer than 16 characters.</p>
				</fieldset>

				<!-- Recipient -->
				<fieldset class="grid gap-4 border-t border-hairline pt-6">
					<legend class="float-left text-[1.0625rem] font-semibold text-ink">3. Bill to (recipient)</legend>
					<div class="clear-both">
						<label for="recipient-name" class="field-label">Name</label>
						<input id="recipient-name" name="recipient.name" type="text" class="field" placeholder="Client or company name" />
					</div>
					<div>
						<label for="recipient-address" class="field-label">Address</label>
						<textarea id="recipient-address" name="recipient.address" rows="2" class="field" placeholder="Street, city, PIN"></textarea>
					</div>
					<div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
						<div>
							<label for="recipient-state" class="field-label">State</label>
							<select id="recipient-state" name="recipient.stateCode" class="field">
								{STATES.map((s) => <option value={s.code}>{s.name} ({s.code})</option>)}
							</select>
						</div>
						<div>
							<label for="recipient-gstin" class="field-label">Recipient GSTIN <span class="font-normal text-ink-3">(if registered)</span></label>
							<input id="recipient-gstin" name="recipient.gstin" type="text" class="field font-mono uppercase" maxlength="15" placeholder="Optional" spellcheck="false" />
						</div>
					</div>
				</fieldset>

				<!-- Items -->
				<fieldset class="grid gap-4 border-t border-hairline pt-6">
					<legend class="float-left text-[1.0625rem] font-semibold text-ink">4. Items</legend>
					<div class="clear-both grid gap-3" data-items></div>
					<button type="button" data-add-item class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm justify-self-start">
						<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg>
						Add item
					</button>
					<div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
						<div>
							<label for="discount" class="field-label">Discount (₹) <span class="font-normal text-ink-3">(optional)</span></label>
							<input id="discount" name="discount" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" step="0.01" class="field tnum" placeholder="0.00" />
						</div>
						<label class="flex min-h-11 items-center gap-3 self-end text-caption text-ink">
							<input name="roundOff" type="checkbox" class="size-5 accent-primary" />
							Round total to the nearest rupee
						</label>
					</div>
				</fieldset>

				<!-- Notes & bank -->
				<fieldset class="grid gap-4 border-t border-hairline pt-6">
					<legend class="float-left text-[1.0625rem] font-semibold text-ink">5. Notes &amp; payment</legend>
					<div class="clear-both">
						<label for="notes" class="field-label">Notes / terms</label>
						<textarea id="notes" name="notes" rows="2" class="field"></textarea>
					</div>
					<details class="group rounded-md border border-hairline bg-parchment">
						<summary class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between px-4 text-caption font-semibold text-ink">
							Bank / UPI details (optional)
							<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
						</summary>
						<div class="grid gap-3 border-t border-hairline px-4 py-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
							<div>
								<label for="bank-name" class="text-fine font-semibold text-ink-2">Account name</label>
								<input id="bank-name" name="bank.accountName" type="text" class="field mt-1" />
							</div>
							<div>
								<label for="bank-number" class="text-fine font-semibold text-ink-2">Account number</label>
								<input id="bank-number" name="bank.accountNumber" type="text" inputmode="numeric" class="field tnum mt-1" />
							</div>
							<div>
								<label for="bank-ifsc" class="text-fine font-semibold text-ink-2">IFSC</label>
								<input id="bank-ifsc" name="bank.ifsc" type="text" class="field mt-1 font-mono uppercase" maxlength="11" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" />
							</div>
							<div>
								<label for="bank-upi" class="text-fine font-semibold text-ink-2">UPI ID</label>
								<input id="bank-upi" name="bank.upi" type="text" class="field mt-1" placeholder="name@bank" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="none" autocomplete="off" />
							</div>
						</div>
					</details>
				</fieldset>

				<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-t border-hairline pt-5">
					<label class="flex min-h-11 items-center gap-3 text-caption text-ink">
						<input name="keepDraft" type="checkbox" class="size-5 accent-primary" />
						Keep a draft in this browser
					</label>
					<button type="button" data-clear-draft class="text-caption text-ink-2 underline decoration-hairline-strong underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink">Clear draft &amp; reset</button>
				</div>
				<p class="-mt-4 text-fine text-ink-3">Drafts are stored only in your browser’s local storage. Nothing is sent to VendorDesk.</p>
			</form>

			<!-- Preview -->
			<div class="grid gap-4 lg:sticky lg:top-20">
				<div class="card overflow-hidden">
					<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-hairline px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">
						<h3 class="text-[1.0625rem] font-semibold">Document preview</h3>
						<p class="tnum text-caption text-ink-2">Total <span class="font-semibold text-ink" data-out="total">₹0.00</span></p>
					</div>
					<div id="doc-viewport" class="overflow-hidden bg-parchment p-3 sm:p-6">
						<div id="doc-scaler" class="origin-top-left">
							<!-- A4 document. Plain CSS with hex colours only: html2canvas cannot parse modern colour functions. -->
							<div id="bos-document" class="bos">
								<header class="bos-header bos-block">
									<div>
										<h2 class="bos-title">Bill of Supply</h2>
										<p class="bos-subtitle">Not a tax invoice · No GST charged on this supply</p>
										<p class="bos-declaration" data-doc="declaration"></p>
									</div>
									<table class="bos-meta">
										<tbody>
											<tr><th>Bill No.</th><td data-doc="bill.number"></td></tr>
											<tr><th>Date</th><td data-doc="bill.date"></td></tr>
											<tr><th>Place of supply</th><td data-doc="bill.placeOfSupply"></td></tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
								</header>

								<section class="bos-parties bos-block">
									<div class="bos-party">
										<h3>From</h3>
										<p class="bos-name" data-doc="supplier.name"></p>
										<p class="bos-pre" data-doc="supplier.address"></p>
										<p data-doc="supplier.stateLine"></p>
										<p data-doc="supplier.gstin"></p>
										<p data-doc="supplier.pan"></p>
										<p data-doc="supplier.contact"></p>
									</div>
									<div class="bos-party">
										<h3>Bill to</h3>
										<p class="bos-name" data-doc="recipient.name"></p>
										<p class="bos-pre" data-doc="recipient.address"></p>
										<p data-doc="recipient.stateLine"></p>
										<p data-doc="recipient.gstin"></p>
									</div>
								</section>

								<table class="bos-items">
									<thead>
										<tr>
											<th>#</th>
											<th class="desc">Description</th>
											<th>HSN / SAC</th>
											<th class="num">Qty</th>
											<th class="num">Rate</th>
											<th class="num">Amount</th>
										</tr>
									</thead>
									<tbody data-doc-items></tbody>
								</table>

								<section class="bos-totals bos-block">
									<table>
										<tbody>
											<tr><th>Subtotal</th><td data-doc="subtotal"></td></tr>
											<tr data-doc-row="discount" hidden><th>Discount</th><td data-doc="discount"></td></tr>
											<tr data-doc-row="roundOff" hidden><th>Round off</th><td data-doc="roundOff"></td></tr>
											<tr class="bos-total"><th>Total</th><td data-doc="total"></td></tr>
										</tbody>
									</table>
								</section>
								<p class="bos-words bos-block"><span>Amount in words:</span> <strong data-doc="words"></strong></p>

								<section class="bos-footer bos-block">
									<div class="bos-notes">
										<h4>Notes</h4>
										<p class="bos-pre" data-doc="notes"></p>
										<div data-doc-block="bank" hidden>
											<h4>Payment details</h4>
											<p class="bos-pre" data-doc="bank"></p>
										</div>
									</div>
									<div class="bos-sign">
										<p data-doc="signatory"></p>
										<div class="bos-sign-line"></div>
										<p>Authorised signatory</p>
									</div>
								</section>
								<p class="bos-fine">This is a Bill of Supply under the CGST Rules, 2017. No input tax credit is available on this document. Generated with vendordesk.tools</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-hairline px-4 py-3 sm:px-5">
						<button type="button" data-download-pdf class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">
							<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11m0 0 4-4m-4 4-4-4M5 20h14"></path></svg>
							Download PDF
						</button>
						<button type="button" data-print class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm">Print</button>
						<p id="bos-status" class="ml-auto text-fine text-ink-2" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="card p-5 sm:p-6">
					<p class="eyebrow">Compliance check</p>
					<div id="readiness" class="mt-3 grid gap-2 text-caption [&>p]:rounded-md [&>p]:border [&>p]:px-3.5 [&>p]:py-2.5 [&>p[data-kind=ok]]:border-success/40 [&>p[data-kind=ok]]:text-success [&>p[data-kind=missing]]:border-hairline [&>p[data-kind=missing]]:text-ink-2 [&>p[data-kind=warn]]:border-danger/40 [&>p[data-kind=warn]]:text-danger" aria-live="polite"></div>
					<p id="bos-dynamic" class="mt-4 text-caption text-ink-2"></p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Mobile action bar (fixed; lives inside the tool root so the script can bind it) -->
			<div class="fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-40 border-t border-hairline bg-parchment/90 px-5 py-3 backdrop-blur-xl lg:hidden" style="padding-bottom: max(0.75rem, env(safe-area-inset-bottom))">
				<div class="mx-auto flex max-w-page items-center justify-between gap-4">
					<p class="tnum text-caption text-ink-2">Total <span class="text-[1.0625rem] font-semibold text-ink" data-out="total">₹0.00</span></p>
					<button type="button" data-download-pdf class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Download PDF</button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Item row template -->
			<template id="item-row-template">
			<div data-item-row class="grid gap-2 rounded-md border border-hairline bg-parchment p-3">
				<div class="flex items-center justify-between">
					<span class="text-fine font-semibold text-ink-2">Item <span data-item-index>1</span></span>
					<button type="button" data-remove-item class="press inline-flex min-h-8 items-center gap-1 rounded-full px-2 text-fine text-ink-2 hover:text-danger disabled:opacity-40" aria-label="Remove item">
						<svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"></path></svg>
						Remove
					</button>
				</div>
				<div>
					<label data-for="description" class="sr-only">Description</label>
					<input data-item-field="description" type="text" class="field" placeholder="Description of goods or services" />
				</div>
				<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_0.8fr_0.9fr_1fr]">
					<div>
						<label data-for="hsn" class="text-fine text-ink-2">HSN / SAC</label>
						<input data-item-field="hsn" type="text" class="field tnum mt-1" placeholder="Optional" />
					</div>
					<div>
						<label data-for="qty" class="text-fine text-ink-2">Qty</label>
						<input data-item-field="qty" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" step="any" class="field tnum mt-1" />
					</div>
					<div>
						<label data-for="unit" class="text-fine text-ink-2">Unit</label>
						<select data-item-field="unit" class="field mt-1">
							{ITEM_UNITS.map((u) => <option value={u}>{u}</option>)}
						</select>
					</div>
					<div>
						<label data-for="rate" class="text-fine text-ink-2">Rate (₹)</label>
						<input data-item-field="rate" type="number" inputmode="decimal" min="0" step="0.01" class="field tnum mt-1" placeholder="0.00" />
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="tnum text-right text-caption text-ink-2">Amount <span class="font-semibold text-ink" data-item-amount>₹0.00</span></p>
			</div>
		</template>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Editorial content -->
	<section class="bg-canvas">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-prose px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24">
			<div class="rich-text">
				<p class="eyebrow">The rules, explained</p>
				<h2 class="mt-3!">When must an Indian business issue a Bill of Supply instead of a Tax Invoice?</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					Under the GST law, the document you hand to a customer tells them — and the tax department — whether tax was charged
					and whether they can claim credit for it. Choosing the wrong one is one of the most common compliance slips small
					suppliers make. Here is where the line falls.
				</p>

				<h3>What a Bill of Supply is</h3>
				<p>
					Section 31(3)(c) of the CGST Act, 2017 requires a registered person who is supplying exempted goods or services, or who
					is paying tax under the composition scheme, to issue a <strong>bill of supply</strong> instead of a tax invoice. Rule 49
					of the CGST Rules then prescribes what that document must contain. The defining feature is simple: a bill of supply
					<strong>shows no tax</strong>. There is no CGST, SGST or IGST column, no tax rate and no tax amount, and the recipient
					cannot claim any input tax credit against it.
				</p>

				<h3>Tax Invoice vs. Bill of Supply at a glance</h3>
				<div class="table-wrap">
					<table>
						<thead>
							<tr><th>Point</th><th>Tax Invoice</th><th>Bill of Supply</th></tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody>
							<tr><td>Issued for</td><td>Taxable supplies by a regular registered person</td><td>Exempt, nil-rated or non-taxable supplies; all supplies by composition dealers; supplies by unregistered persons (as a plain bill)</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Tax shown</td><td>Yes — rate and amount of CGST/SGST or IGST</td><td>No tax column at all</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Input tax credit for buyer</td><td>Available if conditions are met</td><td>Not available</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Governing rule</td><td>Rule 46</td><td>Rule 49</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Mandatory declaration</td><td>None specific</td><td>Composition dealers: “Composition taxable person, not eligible to collect tax on supplies”</td></tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>

				<h2>The three situations that call for a Bill of Supply</h2>
				<h3>1. You are a composition dealer</h3>
				<p>
					The composition scheme under Section 10 lets small businesses — manufacturers, traders and restaurants with aggregate
					turnover up to ₹1.5 crore (₹75 lakh in certain special-category states), and service providers up to ₹50 lakh under
					Section 10(2A) — pay GST at a flat rate on their own turnover instead of on each sale. In exchange, they
					<strong>may not collect tax from customers</strong> and may not claim input tax credit. Every sale they make must
					therefore be documented on a bill of supply, with their GSTIN and the prescribed declaration printed at the top.
					Composition dealers are also barred from making inter-state outward supplies of goods, which is why the generator
					warns you if the place of supply is in a different state.
				</p>

				<h3>2. You are supplying exempt or nil-rated goods or services</h3>
				<p>
					A regular registered person selling fresh produce, unbranded grains, educational or healthcare services, or anything
					else that is exempt or attracts a nil rate, has nothing to charge and must issue a bill of supply for those items. If a
					single sale mixes taxable and exempt items and the buyer is unregistered, Rule 46A allows one combined
					<strong>“invoice-cum-bill of supply”</strong>.
				</p>

				<h3>3. You are not registered under GST at all</h3>
				<p>
					Freelancers, home businesses and small retail suppliers whose aggregate turnover is below the registration threshold —
					₹40 lakh for goods and ₹20 lakh for services in most states, halved in special-category states — are not required to
					register. An unregistered person <strong>cannot charge GST under any circumstances</strong>; collecting tax without
					registration is an offence under Section 32. The GST Rules technically define the bill of supply for registered
					persons, so what an unregistered vendor issues is a plain bill that behaves exactly like one: no GSTIN, no tax, and a
					clear note that the supplier is unregistered. That is what this generator produces in “Not registered” mode, and it
					is what most customers, accountants and marketplaces expect to see.
				</p>

				<h2>What Rule 49 says the document must contain</h2>
				<ol>
					<li>Name, address and GSTIN of the supplier (GSTIN not applicable to unregistered vendors).</li>
					<li>A consecutive serial number, unique for the financial year, of up to 16 characters (letters, numerals, hyphens and slashes).</li>
					<li>Date of issue.</li>
					<li>Name, address and GSTIN or UIN of the recipient, if registered.</li>
					<li>HSN code for goods or SAC for services, to the extent required for your turnover band.</li>
					<li>Description of the goods or services.</li>
					<li>Value of the supply, taking into account any discount or abatement.</li>
					<li>Signature or digital signature of the supplier or an authorised representative.</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					The generator lays out every one of these fields, adds the place of supply (useful for inter-state checks and for
					your own records), and writes the total in words using the Indian lakh-and-crore system so the figure cannot be
					misread.
				</p>

				<h2>Small-value supplies and the ₹200 rule</h2>
				<p>
					Rule 49 borrows the relaxations in Rule 46: a registered person need not issue a bill of supply where the value of the
					supply is <strong>less than ₹200</strong>, the recipient is not registered and does not ask for one — provided a
					consolidated bill of supply is issued at the close of each day covering all such sales. A document issued under any
					other law (for example a receipt under a state VAT law for alcohol) is treated as a bill of supply for GST purposes.
				</p>

				<h2>Mistakes to avoid</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Titling it “Tax Invoice”.</strong> The heading itself signals that tax was charged. Use “Bill of Supply”.</li>
					<li><strong>Adding a GST line while unregistered.</strong> Even a “0%” line invites questions; leave tax out entirely.</li>
					<li><strong>Dropping the composition declaration.</strong> It is mandatory on every bill a composition dealer issues.</li>
					<li><strong>Restarting serial numbers mid-year.</strong> Serial numbers must run consecutively through the financial year.</li>
					<li><strong>Inter-state sales under composition.</strong> Not permitted for goods; check before you ship across a border.</li>
					<li><strong>Losing the copy.</strong> Section 36 requires records to be kept for 72 months from the due date of the annual return for that year — download and file every PDF.</li>
				</ul>

				<p class="callout">
					This page is general information, not tax advice. Thresholds and rules change; confirm your position with a chartered
					accountant or GST practitioner before issuing documents. VendorDesk is not liable for tax auditing errors — see our
					<a href="/terms-of-service">terms of service</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

